{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Winter wheat N × irrigation × seeding trial",
  "notes": "Agronomy trial at a research station: 48 plots of 12 m × 2 m on three fields (North, River and Hill, 16 plots each), harvest 2026. Nitrogen rate (split into two dressings), irrigation level (drip, as % of crop evapotranspiration), seeding density and variety vary between plots. The fields differ in soil type, so the field enters the design as an environmental factor with known values. Soil moisture at sowing (TDR probe, 0–30 cm) and pre-plant soil mineral nitrate (0–90 cm cores) were measured on every plot before any treatment. Grain yield is reported at 15 % moisture; protein by NIR on a grain subsample. Plot H-11 was hit by hail on 14 June and is excluded. Questions: which nitrogen rate pays off on each field, and does the best rate depend on the residual soil nitrate?",
  "factors": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "symbol": "A",
      "name": "Nitrogen rate",
      "units": "kg N/ha",
      "kind": {
        "type": "continuous",
        "low": 0.0,
        "high": 240.0
      },
      "role": "controlled"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "symbol": "B",
      "name": "Irrigation",
      "units": "% ETc",
      "kind": {
        "type": "continuous",
        "low": 40.0,
        "high": 100.0
      },
      "role": "controlled"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "symbol": "C",
      "name": "Seeding density",
      "units": "seeds/m²",
      "kind": {
        "type": "discrete",
        "levels": [
          250.0,
          350.0,
          450.0
        ]
      },
      "role": "controlled"
    },
    {
